          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Joe S"
            },
            "reviewBody": "A little sweet but the rice vinegar added a little bite to it. Tastes like a home made version of many sauces you get in Chinese food. Easy to make. I did separate the stalks from the leaves and, chopped them up in one inch pieces and boiled separately. The stalks took almost 8 minutes, but the leaves should be blanched (one minute tops) or they will shrivel down to nothing. Will make again.",
            "datePublished": "2023-10-31T17:29:30.794Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gail A"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added 1 chopped green pepper, 1/2 cup baby carrots, changed soy sauce to 1/3 cup and added 1 cup of chicken broth. Was really good! The red pepper flakes really added zing to this dish.",
            "datePublished": "2020-03-21T22:39:18.390Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Larry F"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good. Best described as \"broccoli with sweet, tangy sauce\". I served the sauce as a dip, on the side of the broccoli. After making it twice, I made a few small changes: 1 garlic clove instead of 2, and 1/2 T sesame oil instead of 1 T - seemed like too much oil for healthy steamed vegetables. Most importantly, I cut the 1 T corn starch to 1 tsp, because the sauce is plenty thick with just a pinch of corn starch, and way too thick and gooey with a full T.",
            "datePublished": "2019-01-22T04:49:51.850Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lace"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great combination of flavors for Gai Lan. I didn't boil it, just sauted in a bit of oil before adding the sauce. I added a cubed small kohlrabi as well.",
            "datePublished": "2010-12-02T15:32:49.553Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
